A unary `!` over a true-making static comparison, as an operand of an OR
nested under an AND. Reference Tempo evaluates the folded Static there: the
OR is true for every span, so the answer is the Client spans the AND's other
operand matches. Dropping the NOT as the OR's identity element would match
no span (Server and Client at once).

-- query.traceql --
{ (kind = server || !("a" = "b")) && kind = client }
-- seed --
CREATE TABLE otel_traces (
    SpanId String,
    SpanKind String,
    TraceId String
) ENGINE = MergeTree ORDER BY SpanId;
INSERT INTO otel_traces (SpanId, SpanKind, TraceId) VALUES
    ('aaaa', 'Server', 'a0000000000000000000000000000001'),
    ('bbbb', 'Client', 'a0000000000000000000000000000001'),
    ('cccc', 'Client', 'a0000000000000000000000000000002');
-- expected_rows --
[]
